    whatTheyDo: 'Inspects food premises, water supplies, waste systems and workplaces, enforces public-health rules and responds to disease outbreaks, most often for municipalities, government and industry. Practising needs a registered Bachelor of Environmental Health, a year of community service and HPCSA registration.',
